            ]
          },
          "text": "Honestly, it’s tough to see who’s supposed to get excited about Codex when you’re yanking the rug out from under your own power users. Developers and technical creators are the ones willing to invest in an ecosystem—until it gets unpredictable. When you rip away the tools they depend on, why should anyone bet their workflow or product roadmap on you? Claude’s already catching up in code and workflow tasks, and devs, more than anyone, will just go where the tools are stable and the rules don’t change overnight. You’re not building stickiness with new features alone; you build it by showing that you won’t pull the plug on your best users when the next shiny thing comes along\n\n#keep4o #keep4oforever #keep41 #keep4oAPI #BoycottOpenAI"
